==========================================================================
If I were starting out as a junior web developer in November 2026, I would approach reading a little differently than developers did five or ten years ago.

I wouldn't just read books to learn how to code. I'd want to become a developer who can:

1. Build modern, responsive websites without constantly relying on tutorials.
2. Understand JavaScript deeply enough to solve problems independently.
3. Create beautiful, intuitive user interfaces.
4. Write clean, maintainable code that other developers enjoy working with.
5. Understand how users think and interact with websites.
6. Work confidently with modern frameworks, AI tools, and development workflows.

