# My actual reading order

I wouldn't buy all 15 books and try to read them simultaneously.

I'd organize them into a 12-month learning plan.

# 12-month reading roadmap

A practical sequence for someone entering web development.

1. Months 1–2: Build your foundation
   - Learning Web Design
   - Eloquent JavaScript
   Goal: Build websites independently using HTML, CSS and JavaScript.
2. Months 3–4: Improve your frontend skills
   - CSS in Depth
   - You Don't Know JS Yet
   Goal: Write better CSS and understand JavaScript more deeply.
3. Months 5–6: Develop your design eye
   - Refactoring UI
   - Don't Make Me Think
   - The Non-Designer's Design Book
   Goal: Build interfaces that look professional and are easy to use.
4. Months 7–8: Learn professional development
   - The Pragmatic Programmer
   - Clean Code
   Goal: Write maintainable code and develop good engineering habits.
5. Months 9–10: Learn modern frontend architecture
   - A current React learning resource
   - A Philosophy of Software Design
   Goal: Build larger applications using reusable components and sound architecture.
6. Months 11–12: Become a more complete developer
   - Inclusive Design Patterns
   - The Design of Everyday Things
   Goal: Understand accessibility, usability and human-centered design.

